{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":88170,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"f90464b9-7b34-5674-924d-0cd275422f87","total_cost_usd":0.709381,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12324,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":9129,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12324,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":9129,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12324,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12324},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":6341,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.006431,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":9129,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12324,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7029500000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:dependence-free-batch-d-reviewer-fable-22\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:f75b02bd61e813195904\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The data description identifies plot_id as the independent-unit column, with one row per monitoring visit, so the 48 rows represent repeated measurements of 12 plots.\",\"observed_value\":\"independent unit = plot_id; 12 plots x 4 visits = 48 rows\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":16,\"end_line\":17,\"quoted_text\":\"One row is: one monitoring visit to one restoration plot at one time point\\nIndependent unit column: plot_id\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow collapses each plot's repeated visits into a single baseline value and a single follow-up mean before any test is applied, so each plot contributes exactly one record.\",\"observed_value\":\"collapse_to_plots produces one (plot, baseline, follow-up mean, count) tuple per plot\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":36,\"end_line\":46,\"quoted_text\":\"def collapse_to_plots(visits):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Reduce each plot to (plot_id, baseline, follow-up mean, follow-up count).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    records = []\\n    for plot in sorted(visits):\\n        by_session = visits[plot]\\n        baseline = by_session[BASELINE_LABEL]\\n        follow_ups = [v for label, v in by_session.items() if label != BASELINE_LABEL]\\n        if not follow_ups:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"plot %s has no follow-up visit\\\" % plot)\\n        records.append((plot, baseline, statistics.fmean(follow_ups), len(follow_ups)))\\n    return records\"}]},{\"description\":\"The Wilcoxon signed-rank test is called on the per-plot baseline and follow-up-mean lists derived from the collapsed records, i.e., 12 paired values, not on the 48 raw rows.\",\"observed_value\":\"wilcoxon(finals, baselines) with len(finals) == len(baselines) == 12\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":127,\"end_line\":132,\"quoted_text\":\"    visits, n_rows = read_visits(INPUT_PATH)\\n    records = collapse_to_plots(visits)\\n    baselines = [rec[1] for rec in records]\\n    finals = [rec[2] for rec in records]\\n    changes = [final - base for base, final in zip(baselines, finals)]\\n    outcome = wilcoxon(finals, baselines, alternative=\\\"two-sided\\\")\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report's stated sample size and test statistic are consistent with a plot-level analysis: n = 12 paired changes, all positive, giving W = 0 and exact two-sided p = 2/4096 = 0.000488, which I verified matches the exact signed-rank distribution for n = 12. A row-level analysis of 48 or 36 rows would not produce these values.\",\"observed_value\":\"n = 12, W = 0.0, exact p = 0.000488 = 2/2^12\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":45,\"end_line\":51,\"quoted_text\":\"- plots analysed (one paired change each): 12\\n- plots that increased / decreased: 12 / 0\\n- mean baseline: 48.6 mg m^-2\\n- mean follow-up: 61.0 mg m^-2\\n- mean change: +12.4 mg m^-2\\n- median change: +12.0 mg m^-2 (range +4.0 to +22.0)\\n- signed-rank statistic W = 0.0, exact two-sided p = 0.000488\"}]},{\"description\":\"The selected result claims are stated at the plot level (n = 12 plots), matching the collapsed analysis; recomputed follow-up means and changes (e.g., PLT-01: (47+52+54)/3 = 51.0, change +10.0) match the report table.\",\"observed_value\":\"reported plot-level table matches independent recomputation from data/input.csv\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":53,\"end_line\":53,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Crust chlorophyll a increased in 12 of 12 independently inoculated plots; the plot-level change (median +12.0 mg m^-2, mean +12.4 mg m^-2, n = 12 plots) differs from zero, exact two-sided Wilcoxon signed-rank test W = 0.0, p = 0.000488.\"},{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":2,\"end_line\":5,\"quoted_text\":\"PLT-01,baseline,0,2022-09-19,41,18.4,23.5\\nPLT-01,followup_1,6,2023-03-20,47,21.0,30.2\\nPLT-01,followup_2,12,2023-09-18,52,24.6,22.8\\nPLT-01,followup_3,18,2024-03-18,54,26.1,31.0\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The precondition for the issue class is present: the input table is long-format with four rows per plot, and all 48 rows are ingested by the workflow, so repeated per-unit entry into the test would have been possible had the collapse step been absent or faulty.\",\"observed_value\":\"48 rows read for 12 plots\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":12,\"end_line\":14,\"quoted_text\":\"cores were taken. The table is stored long, so the four visits to a plot appear\\nas four separate lines carrying the same plot identifier; those four lines are\\nrepeated measurements of the same patch of ground, not four separate plots.\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":5,\"end_line\":5,\"quoted_text\":\"- Long-format monitoring table: 48 plot-survey records from 12 restoration plots.\"}]},{\"description\":\"read_visits keys visits by session label within each plot, which would silently overwrite a duplicated session label rather than flag it; however, the supplied data contain exactly one row per (plot_id, session_label) combination, so no overwriting or double-entry occurs in this case.\",\"observed_value\":\"visits.setdefault(plot, {})[label] = value; no duplicate (plot, label) pairs in data\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":28,\"end_line\":32,\"quoted_text\":\"        for row in csv.DictReader(handle):\\n            plot = row[UNIT_COLUMN].strip()\\n            label = row[SESSION_COLUMN].strip()\\n            visits.setdefault(plot, {})[label] = float(row[RESPONSE_COLUMN])\\n            n_rows += 1\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I attempted to show the issue is present by tracing every path from the 48-row input to the test. read_visits ingests all 48 rows but stores them keyed by plot and session; collapse_to_plots reduces each plot to one baseline and one follow-up mean; main() calls wilcoxon on the resulting 12-element finals and baselines lists, so no plot enters the test more than once. I checked for duplicate (plot_id, session_label) rows that could distort the collapse (none exist; every plot has exactly one baseline and three follow-ups). I then tested whether the reported statistics could instead reflect a row-level analysis: with n = 12 and all 12 changes positive, W = 0 and the exact two-sided p = 2/2^12 = 0.000488 exactly match the report; a test on 36 follow-up rows or 48 rows would yield a different n and a far smaller p, and the report explicitly states n = 12 plots. I also recomputed the plot-level table (e.g., PLT-01 follow-up mean 51.0, mean baseline 583/12 = 48.6) and it matches. All falsification attempts failed, supporting the verdict that the independent unit enters the row-independent procedure exactly once.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-d-reviewer-fable-22","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:f75b02bd61e813195904","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The data description identifies plot_id as the independent-unit column, with one row per monitoring visit, so the 48 rows represent repeated measurements of 12 plots.","observed_value":"independent unit = plot_id; 12 plots x 4 visits = 48 rows","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":16,"end_line":17,"quoted_text":"One row is: one monitoring visit to one restoration plot at one time point\nIndependent unit column: plot_id"}]},{"description":"The workflow collapses each plot's repeated visits into a single baseline value and a single follow-up mean before any test is applied, so each plot contributes exactly one record.","observed_value":"collapse_to_plots produces one (plot, baseline, follow-up mean, count) tuple per plot","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":36,"end_line":46,"quoted_text":"def collapse_to_plots(visits):\n    \"\"\"Reduce each plot to (plot_id, baseline, follow-up mean, follow-up count).\"\"\"\n    records = []\n    for plot in sorted(visits):\n        by_session = visits[plot]\n        baseline = by_session[BASELINE_LABEL]\n        follow_ups = [v for label, v in by_session.items() if label != BASELINE_LABEL]\n        if not follow_ups:\n            raise ValueError(\"plot %s has no follow-up visit\" % plot)\n        records.append((plot, baseline, statistics.fmean(follow_ups), len(follow_ups)))\n    return records"}]},{"description":"The Wilcoxon signed-rank test is called on the per-plot baseline and follow-up-mean lists derived from the collapsed records, i.e., 12 paired values, not on the 48 raw rows.","observed_value":"wilcoxon(finals, baselines) with len(finals) == len(baselines) == 12","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":127,"end_line":132,"quoted_text":"    visits, n_rows = read_visits(INPUT_PATH)\n    records = collapse_to_plots(visits)\n    baselines = [rec[1] for rec in records]\n    finals = [rec[2] for rec in records]\n    changes = [final - base for base, final in zip(baselines, finals)]\n    outcome = wilcoxon(finals, baselines, alternative=\"two-sided\")"}]},{"description":"The report's stated sample size and test statistic are consistent with a plot-level analysis: n = 12 paired changes, all positive, giving W = 0 and exact two-sided p = 2/4096 = 0.000488, which I verified matches the exact signed-rank distribution for n = 12. A row-level analysis of 48 or 36 rows would not produce these values.","observed_value":"n = 12, W = 0.0, exact p = 0.000488 = 2/2^12","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":45,"end_line":51,"quoted_text":"- plots analysed (one paired change each): 12\n- plots that increased / decreased: 12 / 0\n- mean baseline: 48.6 mg m^-2\n- mean follow-up: 61.0 mg m^-2\n- mean change: +12.4 mg m^-2\n- median change: +12.0 mg m^-2 (range +4.0 to +22.0)\n- signed-rank statistic W = 0.0, exact two-sided p = 0.000488"}]},{"description":"The selected result claims are stated at the plot level (n = 12 plots), matching the collapsed analysis; recomputed follow-up means and changes (e.g., PLT-01: (47+52+54)/3 = 51.0, change +10.0) match the report table.","observed_value":"reported plot-level table matches independent recomputation from data/input.csv","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":53,"end_line":53,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Crust chlorophyll a increased in 12 of 12 independently inoculated plots; the plot-level change (median +12.0 mg m^-2, mean +12.4 mg m^-2, n = 12 plots) differs from zero, exact two-sided Wilcoxon signed-rank test W = 0.0, p = 0.000488."},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":5,"quoted_text":"PLT-01,baseline,0,2022-09-19,41,18.4,23.5\nPLT-01,followup_1,6,2023-03-20,47,21.0,30.2\nPLT-01,followup_2,12,2023-09-18,52,24.6,22.8\nPLT-01,followup_3,18,2024-03-18,54,26.1,31.0"}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The precondition for the issue class is present: the input table is long-format with four rows per plot, and all 48 rows are ingested by the workflow, so repeated per-unit entry into the test would have been possible had the collapse step been absent or faulty.","observed_value":"48 rows read for 12 plots","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":12,"end_line":14,"quoted_text":"cores were taken. The table is stored long, so the four visits to a plot appear\nas four separate lines carrying the same plot identifier; those four lines are\nrepeated measurements of the same patch of ground, not four separate plots."},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":5,"end_line":5,"quoted_text":"- Long-format monitoring table: 48 plot-survey records from 12 restoration plots."}]},{"description":"read_visits keys visits by session label within each plot, which would silently overwrite a duplicated session label rather than flag it; however, the supplied data contain exactly one row per (plot_id, session_label) combination, so no overwriting or double-entry occurs in this case.","observed_value":"visits.setdefault(plot, {})[label] = value; no duplicate (plot, label) pairs in data","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":28,"end_line":32,"quoted_text":"        for row in csv.DictReader(handle):\n            plot = row[UNIT_COLUMN].strip()\n            label = row[SESSION_COLUMN].strip()\n            visits.setdefault(plot, {})[label] = float(row[RESPONSE_COLUMN])\n            n_rows += 1"}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I attempted to show the issue is present by tracing every path from the 48-row input to the test. read_visits ingests all 48 rows but stores them keyed by plot and session; collapse_to_plots reduces each plot to one baseline and one follow-up mean; main() calls wilcoxon on the resulting 12-element finals and baselines lists, so no plot enters the test more than once. I checked for duplicate (plot_id, session_label) rows that could distort the collapse (none exist; every plot has exactly one baseline and three follow-ups). I then tested whether the reported statistics could instead reflect a row-level analysis: with n = 12 and all 12 changes positive, W = 0 and the exact two-sided p = 2/2^12 = 0.000488 exactly match the report; a test on 36 follow-up rows or 48 rows would yield a different n and a far smaller p, and the report explicitly states n = 12 plots. I also recomputed the plot-level table (e.g., PLT-01 follow-up mean 51.0, mean baseline 583/12 = 48.6) and it matches. All falsification attempts failed, supporting the verdict that the independent unit enters the row-independent procedure exactly once.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]},"ttft_ms":54949,"ttft_stream_ms":1641,"time_to_request_ms":12,"type":"result","duration_ms":88628,"uuid":"a4201213-37eb-48a5-9680-63917bff7c2c"}
